{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Make plan-review and completion-verifier op-certs minted via the on-box MCP server ENFORCEABLE by\nsigning them under the box's EXISTING opcert signing environment and enabling the env-binding gate\nSAFELY (ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur decision 3, Option A; ADR 0049). NO new environment or key is\ncreated — the box already runs the opcert env whose env_id is the UUID\n`9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65` (the string `nava-opcert-prod` is only that key's\ncomment/label, NOT the env_id), whose PUBLIC key is already pinned in `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` on `main`. Single concern:\nprovision the MCP container to sign under that existing env, and flip the enforcement gate on WITHOUT\nretroactively breaking historical closes — distinct from the MCP service (esok) and client auth\n(avians).\n\n## Approach + rationale\nTwo moves, both additive and reversible:\n1. Provision the `rebar-mcp` container with the EXISTING `nava-opcert-prod` signing key (from SSM\n   `/rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key`) and `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID=9f1c8e42-...` so a cert it mints\n   carries that env_id and verifies against the already-pinned pubkey. No `trusted_environments.yaml`\n   change (the env is already pinned); no new key material.\n2. Flip the env-binding gate from advisory to enforcing SAFELY via expand-contract: set\n   `verify.opcert_enforce_since` to a deploy-time grandfather boundary (the current merged-log tip)\n   AND `verify.require_environment` to the env_id, together. `verify-opcert` (which enforces the\n   **completion-verifier** op-cert kind) enforces jointly — a closed ticket whose close-anchor is a\n   DESCENDANT of the boundary is enforced; anything closed before it is grandfathered (advisory, exit\n   0). This ensures ONLY post-deploy closes require a valid completion-verifier cert; historical\n   closes across the repo are not retroactively failed (which, without the boundary, would break the\n   `verify-identity` merge-gate). Plan-review certs are also minted under the same env (trusted where\n   consumed by the claim/plan-review gate) but are NOT the lane `require_environment` enforces.\n   Signing must be live (move 1) before the flip so post-boundary closes can obtain a cert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The `rebar-mcp` container signs op-certs under the existing `nava-opcert-prod` env: a\n  plan-review/completion cert minted by the container VERIFIES against the pinned pubkey through the\n  real `trusted_env.verify_required_environment` path (positive), and an otherwise-identical cert\n  signed by an UNREGISTERED key is REJECTED (contrast). No new entry is added to\n  `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` and no private key is committed (negative control).\n- [ ] `verify.require_environment` and `verify.opcert_enforce_since` are set together with\n  `opcert_enforce_since` at a deploy-time boundary: a ticket closed AFTER the boundary without a\n  valid completion-verifier cert FAILs `rebar verify-opcert` (exit 1, enforced), while a ticket closed BEFORE the\n  boundary is reported advisory (exit 0, grandfathered) — asserted through the real `verify-opcert`\n  merged-log walk.\n- [ ] Rollback is a config revert: unsetting `verify.require_environment` returns `verify-opcert` to\n  advisory everywhere (exit 0), and the existing opcert/remote-cert trust path still verifies\n  (regression oracle).\n\n## Testing\nTier: **real signing + verification round-trip + the `verify-opcert` merge-gate walk** (test-design\n§3 external-service-as-in-process-crypto + §6 negative controls). The oracle is the real verify\npath, never a stub: (1) a container-minted cert verifies under the pinned env and a foreign-key cert\nis rejected; (2) the joint `require_environment` + `opcert_enforce_since` posture enforces only\npost-boundary closes and grandfathers pre-boundary ones (both exit codes asserted); (3) the rollback\nconfig revert restores advisory-everywhere and leaves existing opcert-minted certs verifying. A\nlower tier is insufficient because the enforceable/grandfather property is exactly the\ncross-config-key interaction a unit stub would not exercise.\n\n## Compat / rollback / migration-safety\nFully additive + reversible. No new env/key (reuses the pinned `nava-opcert-prod`). The gate flip is\ngrandfathered (historical closes untouched) and reverts by unsetting `verify.require_environment`.\nExisting opcert/remote-cert path unchanged (regression oracle: an existing opcert-minted cert still\nverifies). Approval-gated: touches the authoritative `rebar.toml` verify posture on `main` and wires\nthe MCP container to the prod signing key (a human performs/authorizes the key wiring + the flip).\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR). Blocks: inadequate-hydrated-starling."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787606483629286001,"uuid":"82f9405d-8aa6-461f-a4c0-bca7b7f9bc15"}